@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Create an incident (201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Fire",
  "priority": "Critical",
  "address": "99 Rue Imaginaire",
  "description": "Smoke coming from a warehouse (fictional)."
}

### 2. List all (closed excluded, sorted by priority)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents

### 3. List with filters (type + priority)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents?type=Fire&priority=High

### 4. List including closed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents?includeClosed=true

### 5. List only closed (explicit status ignores includeClosed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents?status=Closed

### 6. Get one incident (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/1

### 7. Get a non-existent id (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/9999

### 8. Valid status change: New -> Dispatched (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Dispatched" }

### 9. Invalid status change: skipping steps (409 Conflict)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Closed" }

### 10. Status change on a non-existent id (404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/9999/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Dispatched" }

### 11. Validation: invalid body (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Fire",
  "priority": "High",
  "address": "x",
  "description": ""
}

### 12. Invalid enum value (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Fire",
  "priority": "Banana",
  "address": "12 Rue Imaginaire",
  "description": "Invalid priority test (fictional)."
}